      "message": "It\u0027s awkward to read battery ID and search your table on every call to charger_profile_override(), you might consider doing this only if rv / rc / soc \u003d\u003d 0, which should be in rare cases.\n\nOr can you use board_battery_type here instead? charger_profile_override() should be called from the charger task, so board_init_battery_type() will have already been called. Or are you worried that battery_manufacturer_name() will be unreadable at board_init_battery_type() time (maybe due to cut-off / waking-up battery)? If so, it might be better to change board_get_battery_type(), always return board_battery_type, unless board_battery_type is uninitialized (BATTERY_TYPE_COUNT), and then try to identify it. Then, change lone uses of board_battery_type to call board_get_battery_type().",
